Canadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson won the Nobel Prize in literature Thursday for playful, genre-blending works that fuse the classical and the modern. Artist, podcast host and writer Mia Funk joined France 24 to discuss Carson’s work.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3025cb2-c32c-11f1-882b-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-133457-133701-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3025cb2-c32c-11f1-882b-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-133457-133701-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7edb550-c32c-11f1-a83e-1b5f0dbce404</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:30:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Student protesters 'showing no signs of backing down'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-student-protesters-showing-no-signs-of-backing-down</link><description>
Students who have been protesting classroom conditions in France for days are "not looking like they are willing to back down", says France 24 reporter Claire Paccalin, despite promises by the French prime minister to bring in measures to address their grievances.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/936ba970-c32b-11f1-b522-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-150142-150557-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/936ba970-c32b-11f1-b522-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-150142-150557-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9884a452-c32b-11f1-a3c5-f1d601a73bf7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:23:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category><![CDATA[People & Profit]]></category><title>How long will the global energy crunch last?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261008-how-long-will-the-global-energy-crunch-last</link><description>
High energy prices continue to drive inflation and stoke anger among voters around the world. But with more crude oil flowing through the Strait of Hormuz, and governments releasing more emergency fuel stockpiles, how long will the energy crunch last? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0db88494-c261-11f1-8c0e-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/P-P-TEST.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0db88494-c261-11f1-8c0e-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/P-P-TEST.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e57ed164-c2f0-11f1-8ab6-6d2264dd57a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:05:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Search warrants for former prince Andrew's homes were unlawful, UK court rules</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules</link><description>
Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec3669a6-c320-11f1-9c1d-5564e18e22be</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:09:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg">©  Kirsty Wigglesworth, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>French connections</category><title>Protest culture: Why do French students repeatedly rise up?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261008-protest-culture-why-do-french-students-repeatedly-rise-up</link><description>
France is in the international spotlight as massive student protests show no sign of stopping. Demonstrating is something of a rite of passage for young people in France, a moment when teenagers discover politics and their collective voice. How has this "protest culture" manifested itself in recent French history? And why are some student protests effective at bringing about change and others not? We take a closer look in French Connections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dffe298-c317-11f1-9dd3-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-08-10-2026-11-59-ING17-PGM-N3-Sub-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dffe298-c317-11f1-9dd3-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-08-10-2026-11-59-ING17-PGM-N3-Sub-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd79778e-c308-11f1-bfe2-b7d4eb3d6e2d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:00:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Florence VILLEMINOT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Microsoft brings more AI to PCs as it challenges Apple</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-microsoft-brings-more-ai-to-pcs-as-it-challenges-apple</link><description>
Microsoft unveiled on Wednesday an AI coding model that can run directly on personal computers and new security technology to prevent AI agents from accessing data without permission, challenging Apple's push to bring more AI into personal devices.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ab4964-c31c-11f1-96f5-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-144211-144341-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ab4964-c31c-11f1-96f5-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-144211-144341-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">983ed5bc-c31c-11f1-9a2e-f7517035b462</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:45:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>30 dead in strike on Ukraine bus as Russian attacks intensify</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-30-dead-in-strike-on-ukraine-bus-as-russian-attacks-intensify</link><description>
Thirty people were killed and at least 18 were injured by Russian strikes in eastern Ukraine that included an attack on a public bus, authorities said Thursday, as an intensive pre-winter wave of attacks continued.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bad38e7a-c31b-11f1-81f3-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-131652-131834-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bad38e7a-c31b-11f1-81f3-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-131652-131834-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c04c4a40-c31b-11f1-af5a-6b679bba1a50</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:44:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'They killed her': Evicted pensioner who sparked Spain housing protests dies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-they-killed-her-evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies</link><description>
The 87-year-old whose eviction last month sparked nationwide protests in Spain has died. Maricarmen Abascal was evicted from her home of more than 70 years last month, after it was bought by an investment fund. After news of her passing, some who took to the streets say they believe her death was brought on by the stress of the eviction.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b609e0c4-c31b-11f1-a68c-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-131450-131622-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b609e0c4-c31b-11f1-a68c-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-131450-131622-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bfd803b0-c31b-11f1-9921-11b40c417143</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:43:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>High school student protests continue in France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-high-school-student-protests-continue-in-france</link><description>
#France: high school students continue to protest Thursday in the face of what they say is the government’s failure to respond to their demands. 
 
Follow the fourth day of protests on FRANCE 24 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbbeae5c-c318-11f1-aed3-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Thumbnail-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbbeae5c-c318-11f1-aed3-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Thumbnail-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0539746-c318-11f1-9ff4-11bb5cc625fc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:40:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art</link><description>
Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5640a08e-c315-11f1-8972-1196b899eff1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:29:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France student protests: What measures is the government taking?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-france-student-protests-what-measures-is-the-government-taking</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said in a televised address Wednesday evening that the country could not be "indifferent" to the concerns of protesting high school students, acknowledging that the "anger of young people does not come from nowhere". He denied that security forces have "orders to confront" the young people, and promised the government would present a plan to respond to the crisis at the end of October. But what measures could the French government introduce and will it be enough to calm the protests? France 24’s Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi takes a look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ae223a-c315-11f1-bdb6-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-130320-130806-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92ae223a-c315-11f1-bdb6-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-130320-130806-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">972c23a2-c315-11f1-95c5-1f31f361ff2a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:54:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Conflict in Yemen: What are the Houthis’ aims?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-conflict-in-yemen-what-are-the-houthis-aims</link><description>
Saudi authorities said Wednesday three people were killed in attacks on two of the kingdom's international airports, including in the capital Riyadh, after Yemen's Houthis claimed to have fired on both transport hubs. The Iran-backed Houthis have claimed a wave of attacks on Saudi civilian infrastructure in recent weeks, which came as Riyadh-backed forces pressed a counter-offensive against the group's territorial gains. France 24’s Philip Turle takes a look at what the Houthis aims in the conflict are.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a99cc884-c315-11f1-9e97-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-120655-121138-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a99cc884-c315-11f1-9e97-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-120655-121138-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aeb250fa-c315-11f1-bbf4-3d5ed1db0550</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:52:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Boston Ballet returns to Paris and builds lasting legacy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261008-boston-ballet-returns-to-paris-and-builds-lasting-legacy</link><description>
In this edition of Entre Nous we speak to Mikko Nissinen, the artistic director of the Boston Ballet, which is performing this week at the historic Théâtre des Champs-Elysées in Paris. He tells us what it means to come back to Paris and what the French audience can expect from works by Alexander Ekman and Akram Khan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0fb21b8-c30f-11f1-942d-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19505438416ac786019cdb78-21885903.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0fb21b8-c30f-11f1-942d-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19505438416ac786019cdb78-21885903.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce299ac2-c30d-11f1-9781-8bf97acb7f51</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:51:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Genie GODULA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French teens keep up school blockades despite prime minister's pledge to act</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-french-teens-keep-up-school-blockades-despite-prime-minister-s-pledge-to-act</link><description>
French teenagers blockaded some high schools and marched through cities on Thursday after the government promised to address their grievances about teacher shortages and dilapidated school buildings. Reporting from Paris, France 24's Jamie Smith-Maillet says protesters he has spoken to see the government measures as lacking detail and have vowed to continue demonstrations until concrete action is taken.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb6bd7ca-c313-11f1-80d7-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-120152-120444-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb6bd7ca-c313-11f1-80d7-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-120152-120444-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f032e406-c313-11f1-a201-4db1261a3601</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:48:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>EU trade envoy eyes yawning goods deficit on first day of China visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261008-eu-trade-envoy-eyes-yawning-goods-deficit-on-first-day-of-china-visit</link><description>
The EU's trade commissioner, Maros Sefcovic, arrived in Beijing this Thursday for two days of talks with his Chinese counterpart Wang Wentao. Sefcovic stated his goal of "rebalancing" an "unsustainable trade deficit". One particular area of concern is the auto sector, where Chinese hybrid vehicles have increased their European market share to 25 percent. Also in this edition: Microsoft unveils its new AI-powered PCs in a bid to rival Apple.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3325e2-c311-11f1-bbbd-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2860317366ac788955b0580-74610388.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3325e2-c311-11f1-bbbd-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2860317366ac788955b0580-74610388.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">15a4c5b6-c304-11f1-a79c-a393051716c5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:15:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Maricarmen, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction shook Spain, dies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies</link><description>
María del Carmen Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction from her longtime Madrid home sparked nationwide protests across Spain and unleashed a political crisis, died on Wednesday while hospitalised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6faf851c-c30b-11f1-a865-3f79da3b2fc9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:54:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Palestinians gained 'nothing' from October 7, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261008-palestinians-gained-nothing-from-october-7-egyptian-businessman-naguib-sawiris-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris called the October 7 attacks a "horrible act of terrorism" that brought Palestinians "only destruction", while warning of an "expansionist" Israeli government. He also said that the economic fallout from the Iran war is already "happening", defended doubling his UAE investment despite the regional conflict, and praised Syria's new president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e5a9816-c254-11f1-8186-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-PKG-EN-TETE-A-TETE-SAWIRIS-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e5a9816-c254-11f1-8186-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-PKG-EN-TETE-A-TETE-SAWIRIS-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1da8cd78-c257-11f1-86e8-c5214af9e234</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:12:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">0e7a9bae-c308-11f1-81cb-a576ba4dd349</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:05:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson</link><description>
The Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson on Thursday by the Swedish Academy in Stockholm. Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws from ancient Greek and Roman literature for her works blending elements of poetry, essay and fiction. She will receive 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million) alongside the prestigious award.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8550d60-c2f6-11f1-8765-cfeb110a5623</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:04:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg">©  Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen, symbol of Spain's housing crisis, dies at 87</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 8: Maricarmen, the evicted Spanish pensioner who became the face of Spain's housing crisis, dies in hospital. Also, France braces for "Act Four" of high school student protests against dilapidated schools and poor staff presence. Finally, actress Zendaya sparks a row over etiquette at Paris Fashion Week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a9ddac8-c2e0-11f1-89c2-ed80457c6312</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:35:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>African Union launches continent's first credit rating agency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-african-union-launches-continent-s-first-credit-rating-agency</link><description>
The African Union launched the continent's first credit rating agency on Wednesday, seeking to provide an alternative to the "big three" global ratings agencies as debt burdens weigh on many African economies. The Africa Credit Rating Agency (AfCRA) — the creation of which African leaders endorsed in 2018 — was ​launched at a ceremony ‌attended by African officials in Port Louis, the capital of Mauritius, where it will be based.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/314caac4-c302-11f1-b240-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-224717-224902-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/314caac4-c302-11f1-b240-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-224717-224902-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36a9e8f6-c302-11f1-a486-799c5d3243c3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:31:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eritrean troops reportedly enter Ethiopia’s Tigray region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-eritrean-troops-reportedly-enter-ethiopia-s-tigray-region</link><description>
Eritrean troops have deployed in Ethiopia's northern Tigray region, multiple sources said Wednesday, threatening to turn an internal conflict into a wider regional war. Fighting broke out between the rebel Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) and Ethiopian federal forces on September 23, sparking fears of a return to the devastating 2020-2022 civil war. Ethiopia accuses Eritrea of backing the rebels, and the two neighbours severed diplomatic ties last week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89d5f73c-c301-11f1-a48c-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-224526-224715-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89d5f73c-c301-11f1-a48c-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-224526-224715-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8eb2929c-c301-11f1-89c9-2f0cfa8704fb</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:30:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French astronaut Adenot begins journey back to Earth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-french-astronaut-adenot-begins-journey-back-to-earth</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot along with the rest of the SpaceX Crew-12 has begun its journey back to earth from the International Space Station. The seasoned helicopter pilot was only the second French woman to travel to space and has now broken the record for the longest continuous stay in orbit by a European astronaut. Her splashdown is scheduled for Thursday off the coast of California.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fc0e43e-c2ff-11f1-bdd7-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-104129-104350-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fc0e43e-c2ff-11f1-bdd7-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-104129-104350-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b899a2a-c300-11f1-bc1b-11d81fc06590</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:29:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>More than 30 killed in Russian strike on buses in Ukraine's Kramatorsk as Kyiv targets data centre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-russian-strike-buses-kills-at-least-12-ukraine-kramatorsk-kyiv-targets-data-centre</link><description>
At least 30 people were killed in a Russian strike on two buses in the Ukrainian city of Kramatorsk in the eastern Donetsk region on Thursday. Earlier, a drone hit a data centre belonging to Russian technology company Yandex, causing a fire. 
